  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3226.11 Bus Body: Emergency Doors and Windows",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3226.11 Bus Body: Emergency Doors and Windows.\n\n(a) A bus shall be rejected if:\n\n(1) Any emergency exit is not accessible;\n\n(2) The door release on the emergency door fails to function when activated or opens without being activated;\n\n(3) Any emergency door fails to lock in an open position;\n\n(4) Any push-out window does not function;\n\n(5) The buzzer indicating the emergency door is open does not function; or\n\n(6) The emergency exit instruction decals are missing, illegible or do not illuminate.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
